SPECIFICATION:
  Adds a third control panel to the S34 design to decide whether the observed
  mean-on-variance slope reflects a failed location identity or an attenuated
  estimator.
  Control C: for each pair, that pair's REALIZED variance v_i read from T39;
  generating mean fixed at exactly -v_i/2 so the identity holds by construction;
  shape matched to the real pooled data via a sinh-arcsinh distribution
  (epsilon = 0.2567, delta = 1.5000, calibrated on a 3,000-pair subsample).
  The regression is run on mean_i and var_i computed FROM THE DRAWN DATA, not
  from the generating parameters. That symmetry with the real panel is what makes
  the control informative; computing them from parameters would return -0.5 by
  construction and test nothing.

CONTENTS: one row per panel (real, normal, control_c) with intercept, slope,
  their standard errors, r_squared, n_pairs, cor_mean_var, var_reliability.

HEADLINE VALUES (ledgered SYNC-13):
  slope real       = -0.196599862499929  (SE 0.00100999289459456) [A2_JENSEN_SLOPE]
  slope control_c  = -0.335064495392663  (SE 0.00138872267605652) [A2_JENSEN_SLOPE_CTRLC]
  var reliability real      = 0.757509663267823 [A2_VAR_RELIABILITY]
  var reliability control_c = 0.614400422437355 [A2_VAR_RELIABILITY_CTRLC]

INTERCEPT IS UNINFORMATIVE IN BOTH PANELS: control_c returns -0.588303115227266
although the location identity is imposed EXACTLY in its generating parameters,
which is further from zero than the real panel's -0.220088355622992. No reading
of the intercept is admissible in either panel.

GATES:
  G1: |pooled skewness - (-0.4755)| = 0.0322 <= 0.10: PASS
      |pooled excess kurtosis - 0.7840| = 0.0311 <= 0.15: PASS
  G2: max|mean_generating_i + v_i/2| = 0.00e+00 < 1e-10: PASS
  G3: identical pair counts across all three panels (27,782 each): PASS
  G4: real panel reproduces S34 exactly (slope -0.1966, intercept -0.2201): PASS
  No gate is placed on control_c's realized slope; that value is the result.

